    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/7XNPF/DEQBBWTDLO/library-systems-specialist": {
      "title": "Library Systems Specialist",
      "description": "Library Systems Specialist - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs Library Systems Specialist Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full time Positions 1 Position Published At: 21 hours ago Loading Refer someone Apply Job no: HRC0027935 Category: Professional, HEW 6 Lead system optimisation, engagement and service excellence. Connect people, data and technology to enhance library services Translate customer needs into effective digital solutions. Be challenged and imagine with us As the Library Systems Specialist, you will play a key role in shaping and enhancing the systems that underpin library services, ensuring they are reliable, efficient, and responsive to the needs of our community. Combining technical expertise, business analysis, and a customer-focused mindset, you will collaborate across the Library and University to deliver innovative solutions that improve access to collections, services, and resources. This is an opportunity to influence how technology, data, and insights support teaching, learning, research, and engagement while driving continuous improvement across Library systems and services. In this role you will: Lead the administration, optimisation, and enhancement of the library's collection management systems and platforms. Partner with stakeholders to analyse business needs and deliver customer-focused system solutions and service improvements. Use data, reporting, and business analysis to identify opportunities, inform decision-making, and improve service performance. Provide expert advice, training, and support to strengthen system capability, data integrity, and collection management outcomes. Champion continuous improvement, innovation, and effective use of technology to enhance customer experiences and access to Library resources. About the Library The University Library plays a vital role in supporting students, academics, and researchers, providing a first-class learning environment that fosters collaboration, research excellence, and academic success. With a strong workplace culture and a commitment to innovation, the Library is both a student-facing service and a strategic hub, adapting to the evolving needs of the University community. The Library develops and preserves print and digital collections, supports collaborative learning and research via contemporary and flexible learning facilities and social meeting spaces, and builds the user experience into the design and development of services and programs. Our recognition and support for the changing needs of students, academics, and researchers is exemplified through investment in learning spaces and resources, a client-centred service model that engages staff and clients in ongoing review of service requirements and introducing technology solutions that enhance the client experience. Our libraries are welcoming places where students come to meet, read, study and learn. We operate four libraries across locations at Callaghan, Newcastle City, Gosford, and Sydney. How Will You Inspire Us Your technical expertise, business analysis skills, and customer focus will help deliver reliable, effective systems that enhance access to Library services and collections. Your communication and stakeholder engagement strengths will enable you to build productive partnerships and translate technical concepts into practical solutions. You will bring a curious, analytical mindset, using data and insights to solve problems, drive improvement, and support innovation. Join the University Library team and contribute to creating inclusive and data-informed learning environments that support students, academics, researchers, and the wider community. What We Offer In addition to working for a university that is breaking boundaries, discovering new ways of thinking and cementing a place as a global leader, we offer a range of benefits to our employees to ensure you balance your commitments, stay healthy and work effectively. These include: Salary range from $97217 - $107268+ superannuation commensurate with skills and experience. 17% superannuation, annual leave loading and salary packaging options. Additional University Holiday days, generous personal, life, and parental leave, and additional purchased leave scheme. Discounts on private health insurance, gym memberships, software, travel and more. A range of support and wellbeing programs. Explore more here - benefits at a glance . Your Next Steps If viewing this on a job board other than the University's please click ‘Apply’ (or equivalent) to reach the University's website, where a copy of the Position Description can be accessed. Please download a copy from the Related Documents section before commencing your application. Your application must include: Your resume. A cover letter outlining your motivation to apply for this opportunity. A statement addressing the targeted questions below: Drawing on your experience, what strengths, values and ways of working would you bring to this role? (Max 1 Page) Tell us about a time when your curiosity helped you identify an opportunity, solve a problem, or improve a service. What actions did you take and what was the outcome? (Max 1 Page) Please upload your Cover Letter and response to the requested Criteria as one PDF document. This document should not exceed 3 pages. Applications for this position will only be accepted from those with Australia Residency or a valid work permit. We value diversity and strive to ensure that our recruitment processes are equitable, inclusive and barrier free. If you require and alternative pathway to view the Position Description or to submit an application please reach out to employment@newcastle.edu.au. We also seek to provide a fair chance to all applicants by providing reasonable adjustments where required during the assessment and interview phases of the recruitment process. Contact Us For specific position enquiries, please contact Katherine McNaughton, Manager Collections Experience – 02 40557666 or Kath.mcnaughton@newcastle.edu.au Please reach out to employment@newcastle.edu.au if you are experiencing any difficulties or would like to discuss reasonable adjustments. Closing Date: Tuesday 10 th November 2026@ 11:59pm AEDST Our assessment process Typically, candidates that progress beyond the shortlist stage can expect to undertake the following (minimum) assessment activities as part of the recruitment process: Interview (an ‘in person’ interview will be conducted as part of the process) Referee checks Pre-employment checks as appropriate to the role Our University is committed to creating a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment for every member of our community. This commitment is central to our values and our efforts to build a diverse workforce where everyone can thrive. As part of this, and in alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025 , from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of our recruitment processes. The completion and return of the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form will form part of the pre-employment checks for this position and any offer of employment will be conditional upon review by the University. Our adherence to the Code is about more than compliance—it’s about living our values. Together, we can ensure our University remains a place where respect, safety, and inclusion are non-negotiable. The University of Newcastle acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands within our footprint areas: Awabakal, Darkinjung, Birpai, Worimi, Wonnarua, and Eora Nations. We also pay respect to the wisdom of our Elders past and present. #LI-KG1 Related documents HEW 6 Library Systems Specialist_PD_September 2026 Published on 27 Oct 2026, 2:33 AM Back to top Refer someone Powered by Privacy Policy Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/Q7EBE/K2O8SRJD2A/project-specialist": {
      "title": "Project Specialist",
      "description": "Project Specialist - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs Project Specialist Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full time Positions 1 Position Published At: a day ago Loading Refer someone Apply Job no: HRC0028188 Category: Professional, HEW 7 Bring your project management and change expertise to initiatives that shape the future of our university. Play a key role in delivering strategic people projects that enhance organisational capability and employee experience. Join a collaborative, people-focused team committed to innovation, continuous improvement and meaningful impact. Are you an experienced project professional with a passion for people, organisational change and delivering outcomes that make a real difference? We are seeking a Project Specialist to join our high-performing People Experience team, where you will drive and support a diverse portfolio of strategic people projects and initiatives aligned with the University's strategic priorities. This role offers the opportunity to work across a broad range of projects spanning organisational development, employee experience, workforce capability, process improvement and change management. You'll thrive in a fast-paced environment where no two projects are the same, bringing strong planning, stakeholder engagement and problem-solving skills to deliver successful outcomes. Working closely with leaders, HR specialists and stakeholders across the University, you will help design, implement and embed initiatives that create positive experiences for our people and contribute to achieving our strategic goals. We are looking for someone who: Has experience supporting and managing complex projects from planning and design through to implementation, evaluation and continuous improvement. Can effectively balance multiple priorities, while maintaining a strong focus on quality, outcomes and stakeholder experience. Builds productive relationships and works collaboratively with diverse stakeholders to influence, engage and drive successful project outcomes. Applies change management, continuous improvement and evidence-based approaches to support sustainable organisational outcomes. Uses research, benchmarking, data and insights to inform recommendations, identify opportunities and solve complex problems. Enjoys working as part of a collaborative team, while also being confident operating independently and taking ownership of outcomes. This continuing position is full-time at a Higher Education Worker (HEW) 7 Level and will be based at Callaghan Campus (Awabakal land). About our university The University of Newcastle stands as a global leader distinguished by a commitment to equity and excellence. Our vision is to be a world-leading University for our regions and create a better future for our community and the world. Underpinned by this vision and our values of excellence, equity, engagement and sustainability, the University of Newcastle's Looking Ahead Strategic Plan 2030 outlines our commitment to delivering an exceptional student experience and serving our communities. To learn more about our university, visit Our Uni / The University of Newcastle, Australia . About the Unit This role sits within the People Experience team in Human Resource Services (HRS), part of the Resources Division. The People Experience team designs and delivers programs, projects and initiatives that support workforce capability, organisational effectiveness and employee experience across the University. As Project Specialist, you will work closely with colleagues across HRS including Talent Acquisition, Learning and Development, HR Advisory, Business Partnering, Health and Safety, Wellbeing and HR Systems, while partnering broadly with leaders and staff across the University to deliver strategic outcomes. What we offer In addition to working for a university that is breaking boundaries, discovering new ways of thinking and cementing a place as a global leader, we offer a range of benefits to our employees to ensure you balance your commitments, stay healthy and work effectively. These include: Remuneration from $107268 p.a. + 17% superannuation Flexible working arrangements in line with the University's Flexible Work Policy Salary packaging opportunities Additional University Holiday days, generous personal leave and parental leave provisions Annual leave loading and purchased leave options Discounts on health insurance, fitness memberships, software, travel and more Access to a range of wellbeing initiatives and support programs Your next steps Your application must include: Your resume A cover letter outlining your motivation for applying for this opportunity (maximum 500 words) Responses to the following behavioural questions (maximum 500 words each) Question 1 Tell us about a project you were responsible for delivering where there were multiple stakeholders with competing priorities or perspectives. How did you build support, manage differing expectations and achieve a successful outcome? Question 2 Describe a time when you led or supported a significant change initiative. What approach did you take to help people navigate the change, and what did you learn from the experience? Please upload your cover letter and responses to the questions as one PDF document. Your cover letter and responses should not exceed 3 pages (approximately 1,500 words). For specific position enquiries, please contact Carlie McQuillan, Senior Manager People Experience carlie.mcquillan@newcastle.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 15th November 2026 @ 11:59pm AEDST Our assessment process Typically, candidates that progress beyond the shortlist stage can expect to undertake the following (minimum) assessment activities as part of the recruitment process: Interview (an ‘in person’ interview will be conducted as part of the process) Referee checks Pre-employment checks as appropriate to the role Our University is committed to creating a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment for every member of our community. This commitment is central to our values and our efforts to build a diverse workforce where everyone can thrive. As part of this, and in alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025 , from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of our recruitment processes. The completion and return of the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form will form part of the pre-employment checks for this position and any offer of employment will be conditional upon review by the University. Our adherence to the Code is about more than compliance—it’s about living our values. Together, we can ensure our University remains a place where respect, safety, and inclusion are non-negotiable. We are excited to be Looking Ahead with you! We are committed to a fair, inclusive, and barrier-free recruitment process. If you require an alternative way to access the Position Description or submit your application, please contact employment@newcastle.edu.au . Reasonable adjustments are available throughout the assessment and interview process to support all applicants to participate fully. The University of Newcastle is an equal opportunity employer committed to equity, diversity, and social inclusion. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and strongly encourage women and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander candidates to apply. #LI-KG1 Related documents HEW 7 - Project Specialist - 2026 (002) Published on 28 Oct 2026, 1:57 AM Back to top Refer someone Powered by Privacy Policy Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/Y74PP/295C6J3E4M/senior-devops-engineer": {
      "title": "Senior DevOps Engineer",
      "description": "Senior DevOps Engineer - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window Close this consent banner This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. To learn more, view the following link: Privacy Policy Storage Preferences Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs Senior DevOps Engineer Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full time Positions 1 Position Published At: a day ago Apply I'm interested Loading Powered by Humanforce Talent Refer someone Join our Talent Community Not the job you're looking for? Become a member of our talent community to stay connected and be informed of any new opportunities. Sign up Already a member? Log in Job no: HRC0026239 Category: Professional, HEW 8 Technical leadership role across enterprise platforms in a collaborative, fast-paced environment Design, build and evolve scalable solutions across a modern enterprise tech stack Mentor and guide a small team of developers Onsite position based at Callaghan, NSW Be part of the University of Newcastle’s ongoing digital transformation and take a leadership role across our enterprise technology platforms. The Role Digital Technology Solutions (DTS) is the engine behind the University's technology strategy, delivering cutting-edge digital services to staff and students and enabling excellence in education, research and engagement. As a Senior DevOps Engineer, you'll sit at the heart of that mission. This isn't a single-platform job. You'll work across an enterprise-grade modern tech stack that includes ServiceNow, Dynamics 365, Okta, SailPoint, GitHub, AWS Cloud, Microsoft Fabric, MuleSoft, Atlassian (Jira/Confluence) and more. You'll provide technical leadership in a cross-functional team to diagnose and resolve complex technical challenges, drive platform reliability and performance, and champion continuous improvement across the team. You'll also be a people leader, mentoring and guiding a small team of developers, building their capability, and fostering a culture of innovation, accountability and collaboration. If you thrive on solving hard problems, lifting others and shaping the way technology is delivered at scale, this is your opportunity. What you'll do : Develop and provision software and infrastructure across enterprise platforms, ensuring solutions are scalable, reliable and secure Lead the design, implementation and continuous improvement of AI-assisted development, CI/CD pipelines, automation, observability and infrastructure-as-code practices Investigate, plan and design systems requirements to meet stakeholder needs, then coordinate implementation end-to-end Provide expert advice, guidance and training to DTS and broader University stakeholders on technology platforms and systems Troubleshoot and resolve complex scalability and performance issues across multi-system environments with upstream/downstream dependencies Oversee code and build quality, review deployments, and enforce development standards Ensure platform health through regular maintenance, upgrades, secure coding practices and alignment with University security policies Mentor and lead a small team of developers, supporting their growth through development plans, performance discussions and hands-on coaching Build and maintain strong working relationships with internal stakeholders, managed-service partners and vendors What we're looking for: At least 5 years experience developing on enterprise platforms with complex upstream and downstream dependencies, for example across areas such as enterprise application platforms, cloud environments, or systems integration Demonstrated leadership and mentoring capability, including experience coordinating multiple stakeholders and managing a team of developers Significant hands-on experience applying DevOps practices, including automation, observability, alerting, infrastructure-as-code, configuration management and deployment tooling Strong ability to identify, troubleshoot and resolve complex scalability and performance issues, with solid ITSM experience (incident, problem, change, release and service-level management) Demonstrated experience implementing information security, risk management and compliance controls within enterprise technology environments Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, the ability to articulate complex technical concepts to diverse audiences and build relationships across IT teams, organisation-wide stakeholders and vendors Demonstrated knowledge of workplace obligations and experience cultivating a safe, healthy, equitable, diverse and respectful workplace Nice-to-Have Experience with ServiceNow or Dynamics 365 is valued but not essential Detailed working knowledge across a very broad range of enterprise IT ecosystems This is a full-time, continuing position at HEW Level 8, located in the Digital Technology Solutions department at the Callaghan Campus. About our University The University of Newcastle stands as a global leader distinguished by a commitment to equity and excellence. Our vision is to be a world-leading University for our regions and creating a better future for our regions and the globe. Underpinned by this vision and our values of excellence, equity, engagement and sustainability, the University of Newcastle’s Looking Ahead Strategic Plan 20 30 outlines the University’s commitment to delivering an exceptional student experience and serving our communities. For more information click here – Our University. What we offer In addition to working for a university that is breaking boundaries, discovering new ways of thinking and cementing a place as a global leader, we offer a range of benefits to our employees to ensure you balance your commitments, stay healthy and work effectively. These include: A remuneration of $120677 - $140791 + superannuation commensurate with skills and experience Excellent employment conditions in line with University of Newcastle professional staff conditions. Flexible working arrangements (in line with the University’s Flexible Work Policy 35 hour week 17% super and salary packaging Additional University Holiday days, generous personal leave and parental leave, annual leave loading and additional purchased leave scheme Discounts in private health insurance, gym memberships, software, travel and more Wellbeing programs Your next steps Please visit here for a guide on how to apply for a role. If viewing this on a job board other than the University's please click ‘Apply’ to reach the University's website, where a copy of the Position Description can be accessed. Please download a copy before commencing your application. Your application must include: Your resume A cover letter outlining your motivation to apply for this opportunity A statement addressing the Essential Criteria listed in the job description demonstrating your qualifications and experience with examples. To ensure that your application receives full consideration, it's important to structure and address the selection criteria outlined in the application process. This helps us better understand your experience and suitability for the role. We appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to reviewing your application. Please upload your Cover Letter and response to the requested Criteria as one PDF document. Your Cover Letter and Response to the Essential Criteria should not exceed 4 pages (approximately 2,000 words). Applications for this position will only be accepted from those with Australian residency or a valid work permit. We are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role. For specific position enquiries, please contact Michael Skerritt, Senior Manager, DevOps Engineering (02) 4921 7079 or email michael.skerritt@newcastle.edu.au Having Difficulties? Please reach out to us: employment@newcastle.edu.au Closing date: Wednesday 11 th November 2026 @ 11.59pm AEDST Our assessment process Typically, candidates that progress beyond the shortlist stage can expect to undertake the following (minimum) assessment activities as part of the recruitment process: Interview (an ‘in person’ interview will be conducted as part of the process) Referee checks Pre-employment checks as appropriate to the role Our University is committed to creating a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment for every member of our community. This commitment is central to our values and our efforts to build a diverse workforce where everyone can thrive. As part of this, and in alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025 , from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of our recruitment processes. The completion and return of the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form will form part of the pre-employment checks for this position and any offer of employment will be conditional upon review by the University. Our adherence to the Code is about more than compliance—it’s about living our values. Together, we can ensure our University remains a place where respect, safety, and inclusion are non-negotiable. We are excited to be Looking Ahead with you e are committed to a fair, inclusive, and barrier-free recruitment process. If you require an alternative way to access the Position Description or submit your application, please contact employment@newcastle.edu.au . Reasonable adjustments are available throughout the assessment and interview process to support all applicants to participate fully. The University of Newcastle is an equal opportunity employer committed to equity, diversity, and social inclusion. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and strongly encourage women and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander candidates to apply. #LI-KG1 Related documents DTS PD - HEW 8 - Senior DevOps Engineer_Aug2026 Published on 27 Oct 2026, 3:46 PM Back to top Refer someone Join our Talent Community Not the job you're looking for? Become a member of our talent community to stay connected and be informed of any new opportunities. Sign up Already a member? Log in Powered by Privacy Policy Terms of Service Cookie Preference s"
