    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/APQJF/VM2FTP10UR/devops-engineering-specialist": {
      "title": "DevOps Engineering Specialist",
      "description": "DevOps Engineering Specialist - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs DevOps Engineering Specialist Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full time Positions 1 Position Published At: a day ago Loading Refer someone Apply Job no: HRC0026240 Category: Professional, HEW 7 Hands-on technical role working across enterprise platforms in a collaborative, fast-paced environment Design, build and improve scalable solutions across a modern enterprise tech stack Drive automation, CI/CD and continuous improvement Onsite position based at Callaghan, NSW Be part of the University of Newcastle's ongoing digital transformation and help shape the future of our enterprise technology platforms. The Role Digital Technology Solutions (DTS) is the engine behind the University's technology strategy, delivering cutting-edge digital services to staff and students and enabling excellence in education, research and engagement. As a DevOps Engineering Specialist, you'll play a key role in that mission. This isn't a single-platform job. You'll work across an enterprise-grade modern tech stack that includes ServiceNow, Dynamics 365, Okta, SailPoint, GitHub, AWS Cloud, Microsoft Fabric, MuleSoft, Atlassian (Jira/Confluence) and more. You'll collaborate with cross-functional teams to diagnose and resolve complex technical issues, contribute to platform reliability and performance, and support the ongoing evolution of University technology services and practices. You'll also have the opportunity to mentor less-experienced team members, help lift capability across the DevOps team, and contribute to a culture of innovation, accountability and collaboration. If you thrive on solving hard problems, improving how things work and building great technology at scale, this is your opportunity. What you'll do: Develop and deploy software, infrastructure and tool sets for the build, test and 