    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/FRDXR/0C4ZECZPBJ/student-progression-officer": {
      "title": "Student Progression Officer",
      "description": "Student Progression Officer - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs Student Progression Officer Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full Time - Fixed Term Positions 3 Positions Published At: 11 hours ago Loading Refer someone Apply Job no: HRC0028042 Category: Professional, HEW 4 Make an impact through process-focused student administration Use your eye for detail in a systems and data-driven role 17% super, generous annual, personal, life leave and health & fitness discounts Be challenged and imagine with us Join our Student Progression team and play an important behind-the-scenes role in supporting the student journey. Working under the guidance of the Student Progression Coordinator, you'll provide administrative support across a range of progression activities, ensuring student and program information is maintained accurately across university systems. This is an opportunity for a highly organised administrator who enjoys working with processes, data and systems, and takes pride in delivering accurate, high-quality work that contributes to positive outcomes for students and the University. In this role you will: Provide administrative support to the Student Progression Coordinator and broader team. Maintain accurate student, course and program information across university systems. Complete high-volume data entry and records management activities with a high level of accuracy. Assist with updates to Program Planner and program sequencing information. Process student-related administrative transactions in accordance with established procedures. Monitor and maintain data integrity across a range of systems and databases. Respond to routine enquiries from students and staff and refer complex matters appropriately. Contribute to continuous improvement by identifying opportunities to enhance administrative processes.to projects and continuous improvement initiatives within the School. This is a full-time, fixed-term position until December 2027, and will be primarily located at Callaghan campus (Awabakal and Worimi land). The incumbent however may be required to work at our other campus locations from time to time. How will you inspire us? You will: Bring strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. Deliver exceptional customer service to students and staff. Communicate clearly and professionally with diverse stakeholders. Demonstrate accuracy and attention to detail when managing information and processes. Build positive and collaborative working relationships across teams. Show initiative and adaptability in a dynamic environment. Embrace new systems and technologies with confidence. Contribute to a respectful, inclusive and supportive workplace culture. Work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Take a proactive approach to improving administrative processes and outcomes. About our University The University of Newcastle stands as a global leader distinguished by a commitment to equity and excellence. Our vision is to be a world-leading University for our regions and create a better future for our regions and the globe. Underpinned by this vision are our values of excellence, equity, engagement and sustainability. What we offer The remuneration for this position is Higher Education Worker Level 4 ($77,098-$83,806) +17% superannuation and is commensurate with skills and experience. In addition to working for a university that is breaking boundaries, discovering new ways of thinking and cementing a place as a global leader, we offer a range of benefits to our employees to ensure you balance your commitments, stay healthy and work effectively. These include: 17% super and salary packaging. Additional University Holiday days, generous personal, life, and parental leave, annual leave loading, and additional purchased leave scheme. Discounts on private health insurance, gym memberships, software, travel and more. A range of support and wellbeing programs. For more information on benefits and conditions, please follow this link . Your next steps Important information before you apply: If viewing this on a job board other than the University's please click ‘Apply’ (or equivalent) to reach the University's website, where a copy of the Position Description can be accessed. Please download a copy from the Related Documents section before commencing your application. Applications for this position will only be accepted from those with Australian residency or a valid work permit. Your application must include: Your resume. A cover letter outlining your motivation to apply for this opportunity. We appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to reviewing your application. We value diversity and strive to ensure that our recruitment processes are equitable, inclusive, and barrier-free. If you require an alternative pathway to view the Position Description or to submit an application, please reach out to employment@newcastle.edu.au . We also seek to provide a fair chance to all applicants by providing reasonable adjustments where required during the assessment and interview phases of the recruitment process. Our assessment process Typically candidates that progress beyond the shortlist stage can expect to undertake the following (minimum) assessment activities as part of the recruitment process: Interview (an ‘in person’ interview will be conducted as part of the process) Referee checks Pre-employment checks as appropriate to the role Our University is committed to creating a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment for every member of our community . This commitment is central to our values and our efforts to build a diverse workforce where everyone can thrive. As part of this, and in alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025 , from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of our recruitment processes. The completion and return of the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form will form part of the pre-employment checks for this position and any offer of employment will be conditional upon review by the University. Our adherence to the Code is about more than compliance – it’s about living our values. Together, we can ensure our University remains a place where respect, safety, and inclusion are non-negotiable. Contact Us For specific position enquiries, please contact Meghann Gibbs, Senior Manager Student Progression, on email meghann.gibbs@newcastle.edu.au or phone 02 4913 8254 Having technical difficulties? Please reach out to us: employment@newcastle.edu.au Please note, we do not accept email applications. Closing date: Tuesday, 24 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST We are excited to be Looking Ahead with you! We provide opportunities for all people regardless of their background and experience, and this philosophy is reflected across all that we do. The University of Newcastle is an equal opportunity employer committed to equity, diversity, and social inclusion. Women and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander candidates are particularly encouraged to apply. #LI-CJ1 Related documents PD - Student Progression Officer Published on 06 Nov 2026, 2:43 AM Back to top Refer someone Powered by Privacy Policy Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://www.livehire.com/careers/universityofnewcastle/job/8YDMF/CWLDGAUFYW/senior-manager-quality": {
      "title": "Senior Manager Quality",
      "description": "Senior Manager Quality - University of Newcastle | Humanforce Talent Log in Humanforce LinkedIn Facebook Google Cancel Powered by ‹ Back to all jobs Senior Manager Quality Location Callaghan NSW 2308, Australia Work Type Full time Positions 1 Position Published At: 15 hours ago Loading Refer someone Apply Job no: HRC0028099 Category: Professional, HEW 9 Lead quality management, risk and continuous improvement across a diverse operational portfolio Shape frameworks and strategies that strengthen service delivery, compliance and organisational performance Make a meaningful impact across the University's campuses, infrastructure and facilities services Be Challenged and Imagine with us The University of Newcastle is seeking an experienced Senior Manager, Quality to lead the development and implementation of a comprehensive quality management framework across Infrastructure and Facilities Services (IFS). This is an influential leadership opportunity to shape how quality, risk, compliance and performance are managed across a broad and complex operational environment. Working closely with senior leaders and stakeholders, you will drive a culture of accountability and continuous improvement, ensuring our systems, processes and services are effective, compliant and aligned with the University's strategic objectives. With responsibility spanning the breadth of the University's infrastructure and facilities operations, you will have the opportunity to make a tangible impact on how services are delivered across our campuses and the experience of our staff, students and broader University community. The role Reporting to the Associate Director, Engagement, Commercial and Business Quality, you will lead the quality management function within IFS, providing strategic advice and driving initiatives that strengthen organisational performance and service excellence. Key responsibilities will include: Quality Management: Lead the development, implementation and continuous improvement of the IFS Quality Management System, aligned with ISO 9001 principles and organisational objectives. Risk and Compliance: Oversee risk management, governance and compliance frameworks, ensuring operational practices meet legislative, regulatory and University requirements. Performance and Assurance: Establish performance monitoring, audits and review programs to identify emerging issues, assess effectiveness and drive evidence-based improvements. Continuous Improvement: Lead improvement initiatives and projects that enhance service quality, operational efficiency and the effectiveness of IFS processes. Strategic Advice: Provide expert advice, reporting and recommendations to senior leaders, supporting informed decision-making and the achievement of strategic priorities. Safety and Business Continuity: Provide oversight of safety compliance and performance, and lead risk and business continuity planning to support the resilience of essential services. Leadership and Stakeholder Engagement: Build strong relationships across IFS and the wider University, promoting quality, accountability and a proactive approach to improvement. About you You are an experienced quality management professional who enjoys working across complex operational environments and translating strategic objectives into practical frameworks, processes and measurable improvements. You will bring: Demonstrated experience developing, implementing and maintaining quality management systems, with a strong understanding of ISO 9001. Extensive knowledge of quality assurance, risk management, governance, compliance and continuous improvement methodologies. Experience designing performance monitoring frameworks, audits, inspections and review processes to assess organisational effectiveness and identify improvement opportunities. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret information, identify trends and develop evidence-based recommendations. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare quality reports, present complex information and influence senior stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to lead improvement initiatives, engage diverse stakeholders and embed sustainable changes across an organisation. This continuing role is full time at a HEW 9 Higher Education Worker Level and is located at Callaghan Campus About our University The University of Newcastle stands as a global leader distinguished by a commitment to equity and excellence. Our vision is to be a world-leading University for our regions and creating a better future for our regions and the globe. Underpinned by this vision and our values of excellence, equity, engagement and sustainability, the University of Newcastle’s Looking Ahead Strategic Plan 20 30 outlines the University’s commitment to delivering an exceptional student experience and serving our communities. For more information click here – Our University. What we offer In addition to working for a university that is breaking boundaries, discovering new ways of thinking and cementing a place as a global leader, we offer a range of benefits to our employees to ensure you balance your commitments, stay healthy and work effectively. These include: A remuneration of $140791 - $150846 p.a. + superannuation commensurate with skills and experience Excellent employment conditions in line with University of Newcastle professional staff conditions. Flexible working arrangements (in line with the University’s Flexible Work Policy 35 hour week 17% super and salary packaging Additional University Holiday days, generous personal leave and parental leave, annual leave loading and additional purchased leave scheme Discounts in private health insurance, gym memberships, software, travel and more Wellbeing programs Your next steps Please visit here for a guide on how to apply for a role. If viewing this on a job board other than the University's please click ‘Apply’ to reach the University's website, where a copy of the Position Description can be accessed. Please download a copy before commencing your application. Your application must include: Your resume A cover letter outlining your motivation to apply for this opportunity A statement addressing the Essential Criteria listed in the job description demonstrating your qualifications and experience with examples. To ensure that your application receives full consideration, it's important to structure and address the selection criteria outlined in the application process. This helps us better understand your experience and suitability for the role. We appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to reviewing your application. Please upload your Cover Letter and response to the requested Criteria as one PDF document. Your Cover Letter and Response to the Essential Criteria should not exceed 4 pages (approximately 2,000 words). Applications for this position will only be accepted from those with Australian residency or a valid work permit. We are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role. For specific position enquiries, please contact Beth McDonald, Associate Director, Engagement Commercial and Business Quality (02) 4921 6733 or email Beth.McDonald@newcastle.edu.au Having Difficulties? Please reach out to us: employment@newcastle.edu.au Closing date: Monday 23rd November 2026 @ 11.59pm AEDST Our assessment process Typically, candidates that progress beyond the shortlist stage can expect to undertake the following (minimum) assessment activities as part of the recruitment process: Interview (an ‘in person’ interview will be conducted as part of the process) Referee checks Pre-employment checks as appropriate to the role Our University is committed to creating a safe, respectful, and inclusive environment for every member of our community. This commitment is central to our values and our efforts to build a diverse workforce where everyone can thrive. As part of this, and in alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025 , from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of our recruitment processes. The completion and return of the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form will form part of the pre-employment checks for this position and any offer of employment will be conditional upon review by the University. Our adherence to the Code is about more than compliance—it’s about living our values. Together, we can ensure our University remains a place where respect, safety, and inclusion are non-negotiable. We are excited to be Looking Ahead with you Footer We are committed to a fair, inclusive, and barrier-free recruitment process. If you require an alternative way to access the Position Description or submit your application, please contact employment@newcastle.edu.au . Reasonable adjustments are available throughout the assessment and interview process to support all applicants to participate fully. The University of Newcastle is an equal opportunity employer committed to equity, diversity, and social inclusion. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and strongly encourage women and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander candidates to apply. #LI-KG1 Related documents PD - Senior Manager Quality (Oct 2026) (1) Published on 05 Nov 2026, 10:12 PM Back to top Refer someone Powered by Privacy Policy Terms of Service"
